From f72b294e3308596e5f259aab7e067d3434b13486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Defer automatic turns silently behind the gateway
 queue

Automatic Desktop turns refused by a forwardable canonical ledger keep the
owner-refusal signal but do not emit the misleading takeover error card.
Carry the ledger status through both admission and notification preflight,
keeping gateway-busy retries at 30 seconds rather than doubling to 300.
Unknown ledger state, foreign legacy leases, coordination failures, and the
typed-prompt forwarding path retain their existing behavior.

Five whys:
Problem: a red "This chat is open somewhere else" card appears with no foreign
user. Why 1: an automatic Desktop backend turn was refused SESSION_NOT_OWNED.
Why 2: the same host's gateway durable ledger held started kanban-wake work.
Why 3: gateway FIFO events and Desktop automatic notices reach the same chat
through two runtimes; collisions are expected and resolve when the turn ends.
Why 4: admission surfaced the same terminal error for self-resolving ledger
contention and genuine foreign ownership; typed prompts already forward.
Root (happened): surfacing was keyed on refusal code, not user actionability.
Root (not caught): the prior owner-backoff tests prevented card spam but did
not establish whether even the first card was warranted for ledger contention.
Recurrence: the 2026-10-28 fix reduced 139 refusal cards in 110 seconds to one
per streak, leaving this misleading first card. A takeover interrupting the
gateway's legitimate turn is consistent with lease-lost logs, not established
causation. Gateway-FIFO routing for synthesized events and button relabeling
remain out of scope.

Proof:
Canonical runner: new ledger-card tests failed 4 cases before suppression;
fixed-retry tests then failed 4 cases before status-aware backoff. All 19
focused cases pass, including every forwardable ledger state, unknown state,
legacy leases, coordination errors, fixed repeated retries, and admission
resumption when the ledger clears. Full consumers/check gates run before ship.
